# THE DATABASE CONSOLE, UPSTREAM'S IMAGE WITH ONE PACKAGE MOVED - A TEMPORARY IMAGE (owner, 2026-11-13).
#
# `adminer:6.3.0` (the newest upstream build on 2026-11-13, published 2026-11-06) carries Alpine's
# `libpq 18.6-r0`, and Alpine 3.23 fixed 38 HIGH PostgreSQL advisories in `18.7-r0`. No upstream digest
# carried the fix, so the image scan failed every pull request. The owner chose to patch the package here,
# not to allowlist the advisories and not to remove the console: the base is the SAME digest production
# ran, and `libpq` is the only package that moves.
#
# DELETE THIS FILE, and put production's compose back on `image: adminer@sha256:<digest>` with the
# `pinned` label, the day an upstream adminer image ships `libpq >= 18.7-r0` - Dependabot moves the
# `FROM` below, so the scan of its pull request is where that is seen
# (docs/wiki/legacy-compatibility.md, the patched adminer image).
#
# `--no-cache` leaves no index in the image; `USER root` only for the upgrade, and back to the user the
# base runs as (`adminer`, read from the base's own config) - its ENTRYPOINT and CMD are inherited.
FROM adminer:6.3.0@sha256:3a07decd833c2375ea749aa8018250c1db4859a78bd55354f797bfb591733233

USER root
RUN apk upgrade --no-cache libpq
USER adminer
